what's up ladies and gentlemen welcome  back to talking Thrones for my first  official season 8 update video for those  of you that are new to my channel I just  want to let you know that I will be  making videos all year just like I did  for season 7 I will release several  videos each week and give you as many  updates as possible I love to make  prediction and Theory videos but also  like making videos about the production  of a new season  anytime I receive some new information  about the upcoming season I will let you  know whether its new set locations  filming schedules set photos new actors  casted and pretty much anything else to  do with Game of Thrones I know many of  us are wondering when season 8 will  begin so I will try to answer that  question for you as best as I can today  and I have a few other exciting details  that I think you will enjoy but let's  get the most important thing out of the  way first everybody wants to know when  season 8 will begin so I will give you  the most recent news about the filming  schedule thus far HBO has neither  confirmed nor denied these claims but  The Hollywood Reporter did interview  HBO's programming president and some  other executives from a few other  networks and as far as I know Game of  Thrones will begin filming in October  which is just one month away from today  when they film season 7 they began in  October as well so as of right now we  are on the same schedule as last year  since winter is here in Game of Thrones  they have started filming later than  usual that way they can film during the  winter months  that way it can appear colder with much  more snow on the ground but even though  filming will start in October again that  doesn't mean we will see season 8 in  July because this season will take a  significant amount of more work to  produce season 8 we'll only have six  episodes but a few different people that  work for HBO have said that they plan on  making each episode feature film length  Game of Thrones episodes typically run  around 60 minutes per episode but in  season 8 they are thinking each episode  may be closer to 80 to 90 minutes each  which is great because even though there  is only going to be six episodes if they  are each around 90 minutes long then  that's close to a normal season's worth  of content I firmly believe each episode  in season 8 will look and feel more like  a movie and since Game of Thrones is  turning into this next level television  show cinematically  it will take a lot longer to produce in  post-production we'll give you a quote  from KC boys who is HBO's programming  president and Casey says our production  people are trying to figure out a  timeline for the shoot and how much time  the special effects are going to take  the shooting is already complicated  enough they have to film on several  different continents with all the  technical aspects and the special  effects are a whole other production  period that we're trying to figure out  that is a big factor in all of this  because as the show gets bigger and more  complicated I have to follow the  producers lead and let go of the fact  that we might not be able to get a new  season a game of Thrones  each year they have to do the best show  that they can do and with shows like  Game of Thrones sometimes if you want  the big show and the big scope it takes  a lot longer to make this is definitely  something we have to consider when  waiting for season 8 to premiere they  may take the same amount of time to film  as they did for season 7 but the  post-production for season 8 is going to  take a lot longer what the special  effects team now that the army of the  Dead is south of the wall we're going to  be seeing them a lot more than we have  ever seen them before  and that's the same thing with the  Dragons all of this is done with CGI and  when you are making these epic battles  it can take weeks or even months to work  to create battle scenes with dragons and  thousands of whites plus you have to  choreograph all of the real actors and  extras that are going to be fighting  them if we want to continue getting a  show that is a cinematic phenomena then  we're gonna have to be patient Season  eight will be the last season so I  completely understand if they want to  take their time with this I want the  show to end on a high note just as much  as everybody else when a show ends  poorly it can affect the entire show's  legacy and I certainly do not want that  to happen with Game of Thrones I have  committed so much of my time to this so  I'm praying that it ends in epic fashion  and I want season 8 to blow us away  story wise and cinematically as far as I  know Dane and Dave have finished the  season eight scripts and they have  turned them in so the final season has  its story now we just have to wait for  them to bring it to life I know there  are season eight leaks floating around  out there already but I do not believe  they are real at all I have not read  them all but I was told a bunch of  scenes to me and it sounds fake in my  opinion I think someone wrote them up  themselves as fan fiction because they  knew this  season eight leaks were accurate so they  figured they could pass anything off as  a real leak now but don't believe  everything that you read there is some  other exciting season 8 news that just  came out today thanks to a group of  people in Ireland who follow Game of  Thrones there is a Twitter page called  Irish clones and they are dedicated to  sharing information about the Game of  Thrones locations in Ireland according  to them some of the Game of Thrones sets  are already operational and have begun  preparing to film season 8 next month  one of their tweets says the set in  Corbett Ireland is back up and running  and work is well underway and very busy  the Riverrun castle front is still up  and operational and very busy - and this  is pretty exciting news in my opinion  this must mean Game of Thrones 